Subject: [PATCH] Admit exact INT8 Metal KV mappings for Gemma4 E4B

The published E4B export keeps INT8 KV tensors in external MetalBuffer
storage with the same physical stride16 marker as the existing FP16 path.
Admit that exact signed-byte provider/element pair through the checked
unpadded transfer path. Preserve rank, positive-dimension, stride, size,
index-range and offset validation. Ordinary inference is unchanged.

The matching LiteRT0005 provider patch handles signed-byte transfers and
checkpoint preflight. This codec still requires successful staging cleanup.
Tests cover both admitted formats, all 256 byte values in K/V-shaped
mappings, invalid padding/strides/provider/type/size and prevalidation
before writes. Also correct the stale C API MTP persistence comment.

Base: google-ai-edge/LiteRT-LM 5f25078c9439e176615af5ba42636ed904fca847
Apply after 0001-0012 in the LiteRT-LM patch sequence; requires LiteRT0005.
Artifact SHA-256:
  0b2a8980ce155fd97673d8e820b4d29d9c7d99b8fa6806f425d969b145bd52e0
Bounded evidence SHA-256:
  e4b-shapes.json: e9605ba67361bc1d7fa5e1d82ad93b633ed91f4b40929e457a36413132b09d32
  e4b-ranges.json: 12af31fc70c25251b741f1800fb93039845f5e5c3fd4d09cec8ef6a62f9d86cf

Validation: production codec rebuilt; all 11 existing native parser tests
passed. Updated registered-provider test source passed syntax/type checks
against real pinned headers. Full TensorBuffer tests and native Metal
execution were not run. No hardware claims derive from the fake provider.

